5,1,1,talk,Midori,,"I’m a bit nervous, but I want to understand why past projects stalled. Who else feels the ownership gap is our biggest risk?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Midori, ownership gaps matter, but I’m more worried about physical constraints. The yard equipment is outdated. Can the new system handle our actual depot calendar?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,I’m less worried about hardware and more about how we handle aging systems. Who else thinks we need to check the upgrade history?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I’m concerned about the people. If key staff are stretched thin, the rollout will fail. Who else sees the staffing risk?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I worry about the invoice trail. Why do we assume the headline price covers the full lifecycle? Who else sees the hidden costs?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I hear you on the calendar. But if we don’t know who owns the system when it breaks, the schedule is just a wish.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, ownership is vital, but if the system crashes during peak season, no owner helps. We must verify the depot calendar first.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, I agree the calendar is tight, but ignoring the upgrade history is how we end up with a system that quietly ages in place.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I agree. But if the people running it are already stretched, the upgrade history is just a warning. We need to check the staffing reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, I agree. But upgrade history is just a symptom. The real risk is the recurring fees that outlive the contract. Who else tracks the long-term bill?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But if we don’t know who is in charge when things break, the bill is just a number. Who else feels this way?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, I understand the financial risk. However, if the system fails on the yard floor, the invoice is irrelevant. We must prioritize operational continuity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, I hear you, but recurring fees are just the symptom. The real danger is a system that quietly ages in place. We must check the upgrade history.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if the people holding the system together are already stretched, the bill is just a number. We need to check the staffing reality.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, I appreciate the concern, but staffing is a variable. The invoice trail is a constant. We must verify the renewal costs before we commit to the people.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I understand the financial pressure. But without clear ownership, the invoice is just a number. I’ll look into the support ownership and the depot calendar.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
